{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":56,"timestamp":"2026-07-14T04:39:58.398544539Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"1b2c2eec-f80d-4ec8-b103-5b9faca8c40a","title":"Encode role in allowed_signers principal (role+agent_id@crosslink)","description":"## Gap #3 — Role→Key Binding via Principal Encoding (MEDIUM)\n\nAllowedSignerEntry (signing.rs:498-508) has no role field. The parser at signing.rs:542-604 is hand-parsed (splitn(2,' ')), so a trailing/encoded field is safe.\n\n## What to do\n\n1. Encode role in allowed_signers principal: role+agent_id@crosslink (e.g. builder+agent-7@crosslink)\n2. Parse principal.split('+') for role when needed\n3. Enforce that only the declared role key may sign a given artifact type\n4. Keep AllowedSignerEntry struct unchanged (no breaking change)\n\n## Why principal encoding\n- Avoids breaking ssh-keygen -Y verify compatibility\n- Keeps AllowedSignerEntry unchanged\n- Simpler than adding a struct field + migration\n\n## Source\nto-file/crosslink-gates/gates-issues.md GATE-2.4\ngates-verified-facts.md §2 (AllowedSignerEntry, parser location)","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQO3OEyCG/qbo36DfeUkU+BOhFA6hboSzRFbkB3maf8V5Lhf7WMUgzHVapC6i5VetE8S0PJ9kVFn8rGCZB1k41Qo="}
